@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor transparent
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #2C3E50
    ActorBorderColor #2C3E50
    LifeLineBorderColor #7F8C8D
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #ECF0F1
    ParticipantBorderColor #34495E
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #E8EFEA
    ParticipantFontColor #172126
    BoxBorderColor #BDC3C7
    BoxBackgroundColor #F8F9FA
    GroupBorderColor #27AE60
    GroupHeaderFontColor #1E8449
}

box "Existing Session" #F0F4F8
participant "Client 1\n(Node_B)" as C1
end box

box "Server Internals" #FFFFFF
participant "APX Server\n(File Manager & Sessions)" as S
participant "Routing Engine\n(Signature Map & Connectors)" as R
end box

box "Connecting Session" #F0F4F8
participant "Client 2\n(Node_A)" as C2
end box

== 1. Transport Connection & Greeting Handshake ==
C2 -> S: TCP/UNIX connect + RMFP Greeting (NumHeader: 32)
S -> C2: RMF_CMD_ACK (greeting accepted)

== 2. Definition & Initial Provide Data Ingestion ==
C2 -> S: FileInfo: Node_A.apx
C2 -> S: FileInfo: Node_A.out
S -> C2: OpenFile: Node_A.apx
C2 -> S: FileWrite: Node_A.apx [IDL text]
S -> S: Parse AST, compile VM programs, allocate buffers
S -> C2: OpenFile: Node_A.out
C2 -> S: FileWrite: Node_A.out [Initial provide-data snapshot]

== 3. In-Memory Pre-Population & Port Matching ==
note over S, R #EAFAF1
  **Deferred Publication & Pre-Population:**
  Server completes port matching and prepopulates in-memory buffers
  BEFORE announcing any server-owned files to Client 2.
end note
S -> R: Bidirectional port matching (Node_A <-> Node_B)
activate R
R -> S: Populate in-memory Node_A.in (values copied from Client 1)
R -> S: Populate in-memory Node_A.cin (require connection counts)
R -> S: Populate in-memory Node_A.cout (provide connection counts)
deactivate R

== 4. Orderly Server File Publication (Fully Populated) ==
note over S
  Server publishes files in strict dependency order:
  .cout -> .cin -> .in
end note
S -> C2: FileInfo: Node_A.cout (fully pre-calculated)
S -> C2: FileInfo: Node_A.cin  (fully pre-calculated)
S -> C2: FileInfo: Node_A.in   (fully pre-calculated with initial values)

== 5. Bulk Snapshot Transfers to Connecting Client ==
C2 -> S: OpenFile: Node_A.cout
S -> C2: FileWrite: Node_A.cout [Single Bulk Snapshot]
note right of S #D4EFDF: 1 bulk transfer for all provide counts

C2 -> S: OpenFile: Node_A.cin
S -> C2: FileWrite: Node_A.cin [Single Bulk Snapshot]
note right of S #D4EFDF: 1 bulk transfer for all require counts

C2 -> S: OpenFile: Node_A.in
S -> C2: FileWrite: Node_A.in [Single Bulk Snapshot]
note right of S #D4EFDF: 1 bulk transfer for all require data

== 6. Batched & Coalesced Updates to Existing Peer Clients ==
note over S, C1 #EAFAF1
  Surviving peer nodes enter a batch (begin_batch).
  Disjoint range lists coalesce adjacent updates (max_gap <= 6 bytes).
  Flushed in dependency order (.cin -> .cout -> .in) on end_batch().
end note
group Batched Flushes to Peer Client (Dependency Order)
    S -> C1: FileWrite: Node_B.cin [Coalesced Range / Bulk Count Update]
    note left of S #D4EFDF: Coalesced require count updates
    S -> C1: FileWrite: Node_B.cout [Coalesced Range / Bulk Count Update]
    note left of S #D4EFDF: Coalesced provide count updates
    S -> C1: FileWrite: Node_B.in [Coalesced Range / Bulk Signal Update]
    note left of S #D4EFDF: Coalesced signal data updates
end

@enduml

